From 86f91825948ef83c492150fd3dd08c49e805f11c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:53:07 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 124/152] drm: Add an Exynos9810 DPU takeover KMS driver

The bootloader leaves DECON0 scanning out window 5 from IDMA_G0 (both
DSI links in video mode, SysMMU in bypass). Keep that setup and flip the
scanout buffer: write IDMA_IN_BASE_ADDR_Y and request a DECON shadow
update, latched at the next frame start; vblank from the DECON frame
start interrupt. The driver is called "exynos" so that Mesa's kmsro
pairs it with panfrost, claims the boot framebuffer so simpledrm backs
off, reports a DSI connector with the panel size (for the compositor's
scale and backlight), and exposes the on-screen buffer in debugfs
(scanout) for screenshots.

Tested on the SM-T570: fbcon on the driver's CMA buffer, simpledrm out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
